              "text": "ਪਿਤਾ (pitā) is Sanskrit pitā, the nominative of pitṛ, \"father\", taken over whole, a tatsama. The inherited line survives in Punjabi piu, \"mother and father\", which CDIAL lists under pitṛ (CDIAL 8179)."
